  <static seed="1771" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/Decimal/AddSubtractDecimals15.pg">
    <statement><p>Simplify without using a calculator.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ -1.41 + (-48.4) }</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-49.81</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>When we add up two negative numbers, the result will be negative.</p>
<p>We need to find the sum of their absolute value. To add two decimals, make sure to line up the decimal points:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \amp \phantom{+4}1.41 \\
 \amp \underline{+4  8.4\phantom{ad}} \\
   \amp \phantom{+}49.81
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Since the result is negative, we have <m>-1.41 + (-48.4) = -49.81</m>.</p>
</solution>
